From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: refuse to offload flows behind a shaping qdisc

The PPE entry's shaper-id field is hardcoded to 0x7f, the fqos table's
"no shaper" entry: the driver never programs an fqos table, so every
offloaded flow is forwarded as unshaped, even when the egress netdev has
a tc qdisc that is supposed to rate limit it.  On the XR1710G the
jitter-paced WAN tbf is exactly that case: the cap only holds the packets
that still take the software path, while the flows that go through the
PPE -- the ones filling the slow egress queues -- ignore it.

The offload path never sees an skb: netfilter builds the flow rule from
conntrack, does not pass skb->priority, and the rule carries no per-flow
shaper-id metadata.  With no way to tell which tc class a flow belongs
to, the closest signal is the egress netdev's root qdisc: when it is a
rate limiter (tbf, htb, hfsc, cake, netem, mqprio, cbs), every flow that
egresses there is refused with -EOPNOTSUPP, so the flow stays in the
software path and the qdisc keeps shaping it.  Refusing all of them is
deliberate -- offloading one past the qdisc is the correctness bug, and
the shaper-id field cannot encode an unshaped exception either.

Flows whose egress root qdisc is a queue-management or scheduling qdisc
(fq_codel, sfq, mq, prio, ...) are not rate limited, keep the 0x7f default
and stay offloadable.  No table geometry, BND_AGE, PPPoE or L2B code is
touched.

This is a correctness fix, not a throughput optimisation: a shaped egress
runs through the CPU.  The decision is taken at offload time, so an entry
that is already resident when a qdisc is installed keeps forwarding in
hardware until it ages out; the qdisc-change path has no hook into the
driver.

Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -609,19 +609,70 @@
 					      hwe->ipv6.l2.src_mac_hi));
 }
 
+/* Rate-shaping qdiscs whose egress the PPE cannot represent.  A PPE entry
+ * names a shaper through the fqos table (AIROHA_FOE_SHAPER_ID), but this
+ * driver does not program that table: 0x7f is its "no shaper" entry.  A
+ * flow that the qdisc would rate limit must not be offloaded with 0x7f, or
+ * it would bypass its own limit.
+ *
+ * Read the qdisc attached to the egress device instead of a driver flag:
+ * netfilter passes no skb to the offload driver (and hence no
+ * skb->priority/classid), so the qdisc is the only place the tc shaping
+ * request is visible.  Only rate limiters are listed; queue-management and
+ * scheduling qdiscs do not limit the rate and keep their flows offloadable.
+ */
+static const char *const airoha_ppe_shaping_qdiscs[] = {
+	"tbf", "htb", "hfsc", "cake", "cake_mq", "netem", "mqprio", "cbs",
+};
+
+static bool airoha_ppe_netdev_is_shaped(struct net_device *netdev)
+{
+	struct Qdisc *qdisc;
+	bool shaped = false;
+	int i;
+
+	if (!netdev)
+		return false;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	qdisc = rcu_dereference(netdev->qdisc);
+	if (qdisc) {
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(airoha_ppe_shaping_qdiscs); i++) {
+			if (!strcmp(qdisc->ops->id,
+				    airoha_ppe_shaping_qdiscs[i])) {
+				shaped = true;
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	return shaped;
+}
+
 static int airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(struct airoha_eth *eth,
 					struct airoha_foe_entry *hwe,
 					struct net_device *netdev, int type,
 					struct airoha_flow_data *data,
 					int l4proto, u8 dsfield, bool bridged)
 {
-	u32 qdata = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_SHAPER_ID, 0x7f), ports_pad, val;
+	u32 qdata, ports_pad, val;
+	struct net_device *egress = netdev;
 	int wlan_etype = -EINVAL, dsa_port = airoha_get_dsa_port(&netdev);
 	struct airoha_foe_mac_info_common *l2;
 	u8 smac_id = 0xf;
 
 	memset(hwe, 0, sizeof(*hwe));
 
+	/* Leave a flow that its egress qdisc would shape to the software
+	 * path.  qdata can only name an fqos shaper this driver does not
+	 * program, and the 0x7f "no shaper" entry would bypass the limit.
+	 */
+	if (airoha_ppe_netdev_is_shaped(egress))
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
+	qdata = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_SHAPER_ID, 0x7f);
+
 	val = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_STATE, AIROHA_FOE_STATE_BIND) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_PACKET_TYPE, type) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB1_BIND_UDP, l4proto == IPPROTO_UDP) |
